WEBVTT

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.290
I'm back.
Sorry I took so long.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.210
I finished the Impossible Mission,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.080
but there was a lot that I failed to achieve.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.330
I hope you don't mind me burying you here, Master,
even if all I have of you is a finger.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.460
You're all here?

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.380
There was really no need for everyone to come.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.080
Boss,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.420
the nine of us are a new team called Lamplight,
and we're going to pick up where Inferno left off.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.710
I hope you're watching over us.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.920
<b>20 Days Before the Impossible Mission</b>

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:57.670
In twenty days, we'll be heading to the Galgad Empire
to begin the Impossible Mission.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.880
Until then, I'll continue forging you all into proper spies.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.670
We're going to complete this mission,
and we're all going to make it back alive.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:07.920
...is what he said!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.080
Now, let's come together as a group
and pull out at all the stops to beat Teach!

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.500
Yeah!

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.380
<b>SPY CLASSROOM</b>

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.750
<b>FILE: Fool Erna</b>

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.380
Whaddya say I take point on our next plan?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.670
It'll work, I promise!

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.500
We need to start by gathering intel.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.500
I still think

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.960
our only shot is to discover where he's
vulnerable and blackmail him.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.330
He's a first-rate spy among first-rate spies.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.630
Our best option is to find some way of detaining him.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:04.750
It'd be quickest if I just used my bombs to
blow the whole manor off the map, yo!

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.750
There's just one thing I don't understand.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.170
When we attacked him in the bathroom the other day,

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.580
why wasn't the changing room locked properly?

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.000
I'm sorry, was that directed at me?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.290
I mean, you were the one in charge of lock duty.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.920
Hey, don't look at me.
I sealed it off with a combination lock.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.460
There's no way to open it without the six-digit code.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.830
At least own up to your mistake.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.880
With how bad the attack squad shat the bed,
I don't think you're one to talk.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.130
All right, that's enough.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.130
Teamwork is the name of the game right now.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.580
Here, these'll help you cool off.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.880
Ooh, financiers.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.710
Dang, that's good.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:46.040
If you want seconds, all you have to do
is bow down to your glorious leader.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.210
I do agree that we should work on our coordination.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.830
Yeah, and the bonds between us as friends!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.000
That's what really matters!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.290
Hey, you got anything to add?

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.920
All this talk about "bonds" is just platitudes.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.330
Spies can't afford to give out their trust that easily.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.790
Do you, uh, want a financier?

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.960
No.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.750
I'm going for a walk.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.750
I didn't mean it like that.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.880
I just wanted to remind them that
it's a spy's job to doubt everything.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.500
They keep talking about friendship,

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.130
but I just don't feel that close with them yet,

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.290
especially with how I showed up late.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.630
And plus, if I get too close to them-

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.880
Hey, kid, hold up a second.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.960
Looking at those nice clothes you've got,
I'd say you're a member of the bourgeois.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.040
You mind coming with us?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.290
C'mon, let's be friends.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.080
You can think of it as an act of philanthropy.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.210
Friends?

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.460
Tell me, mister,

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.790
how are we supposed to become friends?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.580
See?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.500
Now you wanna be my friend, right?

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.630
How unlucky...

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:22.670
Huh?

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.380
Can we go this way?

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.830
How unlucky...

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.040
Just as my whole life has been.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.170
Huh?

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:43.710
I get dragged into them day in and day out...

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.420
Accidents, tragedies, calamities...

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.000
What're you muttering about?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.250
But it's let me kind of sense them.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.960
I can tell when and where misfortune will strike.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.630
I'm code name Fool,

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.420
and it's time to kill with everything.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.080
Goodbye, mister.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.130
Your clothes are a mess!
What happened?!

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.580
I'll carry out the next attack solo.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.500
I want the rest of you to help from the sidelines.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.540
Are...

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.630
Are you sure you can handle it?

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.920
She'll be fine, yo!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.790
We went to the same academy for a while,

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.290
so I know the rumors!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.330
Wh-what are you talking about?

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:47.000
Erna's a really unlucky girl!

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.750
That's why she'll be fine!

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.000
Unlucky?

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.460
I don't see what's fine about that at all.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.750
Someone I knew got into an accident, yo.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.000
That's why our friend here got transferred!

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.500
Right?

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Huh?

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:18.170
<i>Bad things happen to the people around me.</i>

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.540
<i>And if they died, it was written off as an accident.</i>

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.040
<i>The way I specialize in accidents and misfortune</i>

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.880
<i>makes me the perfect assassin.</i>

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.080
<i>I'm...</i>

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.170
<i>I'm a horrible person.</i>

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.580
<i>I'll overpower Teach.</i>

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:48.500
<i>Then, everyone will respect me
and compliment me and not abandon me...</i>

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:52.460
<i>This time, I'm going to become
proper friends with the group.</i>

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.380
Teach, what a coincidence.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.210
Lily tripped over my paints last night,
so I had to replace them.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.790
Is it just you?

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:19.170
It's my turn to go shopping for the group.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:22.920
Everyone else is training
to get ready for the next attack.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.960
I'll be sure to look forward to it.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.380
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.960
<i>I need to keep the conversation going
so I can lure him in!</i>

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.880
What is it you're buying?

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.670
On your shopping-

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:44.750
Gr-groceries, and soap, and an alarm clock.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.080
One of the curtains got torn, so a little bit of fabric.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.040
And if I find something cute,
I might get a new set of pajamas.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.580
That sounds like a lot to carry on your own.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:53.880
I'll come help.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.670
Where to first?

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.670
I want to go to the clothing store on Main Street.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:04.830
Got it.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:10.330
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.040
<i>You're about to be struck by misfortune, Teach.</i>

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.000
Well, that was dangerous.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.040
Are you all right?

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.290
T-Teach, you're okay?

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:47.500
Never better.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.670
I punctured its tire.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:52.420
If it had kept on going like that,
it could have killed someone.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.080
But it happened so fast...

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:56.380
The police can handle the rest.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.630
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:06.830
<i>I still smell more misfortune.</i>

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:07.960
<i>Yeep!</i>

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:26.420
Oh dear, this one got chipped.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:30.040
<i>He's an actual, factual monster!</i>

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.540
I believe that's the last item from your list.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.080
Th-that's right.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.080
But there are still places I want to-

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.080
I think this farce has gone on long enough.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.630
The teachers at your academy told me
about your ability.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.170
They called you a girl who attracts misfortune.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.170
You have a predisposition for bad luck.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.420
At least, that's how I'm referring to it
for the sake of convenience.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.080
No condition that unscientific actually exists,

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.750
so perhaps I should call it intropunitive ideation.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:04.420
I remember hearing about that mansion fire,

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:07.170
and about the young girl who was its sole survivor.

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:13.290
The incident made you fixated on the idea
that it was unfair that only you got to live.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.540
So, you seek out punishment.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:20.080
Your subconscious sniffs out misfortune
and guides you towards it.

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:28.540
I knew it, I am a horrible person.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:33.920
People really misunderstand you.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.000
I'll tell you what's really unlucky:

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.750
that a girl with your talents never got
the respect she deserved for them.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.790
You've done well.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.330
The way I see it, you're the luckiest girl there is.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.540
Yeep?

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.500
A lot of people all got saved thanks to you.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:55.040
That runaway car could have hit another pedestrian.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:59.170
The people on the street could have been
splashed when that stew fell over.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:01.380
The mad dog could have bitten a child,

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.460
and the bricks could have fallen on that woman.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.080
I'm bad luck and an ill omen and detestable!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:12.040
You've been spending time with a demon
who drowns people in misfortune!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.710
Well, I certainly haven't been drowned.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.290
But...

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.540
What's wrong?
Are you crying?

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:22.920
I...

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.130
You?

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:25.960
I'm not crying!

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.170
What is it?

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.290
I-it's nothing...

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:37.790
<i>If I tell him, Teach might leave me.</i>

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.500
<i>But...</i>

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.710
<i>since it's him...</i>

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:54.710
Teach, would you mind following me?

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.080
<b>FILE: Fool Erna</b>

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:10.500
I assume you're aware, Erna, but we're surrounded.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.830
Who's there?

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:24.000
Don't move an inch.
We've got a hostage.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:28.500
No way a councilman's daughter runs away
and leaves a constituent to die, yeah?

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:32.670
You can play dumb all you want,
but we already know exactly who you are.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.250
What's going on?

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.460
I don't know.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:38.290
They seem to have us confused for someone else,
but I doubt we can convince them of that.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.210
Can you take them out?

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:43.540
I can't.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:44.750
Teach?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:49.130
The part about them having a hostage is true.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.630
We'll have to just go along with their demands.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:52.540
<i>At least my transmitter is still-</i>

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:12.540
We're tied up, there are no windows,
and the guards are armed.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:14.790
Where's the rest of the team?

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:16.710
They were tailing us, right?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.330
My transmitter broke.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.380
Probably because of my bad luck...

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.960
I really am a horrible person...

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.580
I'm sorry, Teach.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.420
This is all my fault.

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:31.380
I always bring misfortune to people.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:34.080
I drag them in, and they get hurt...

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.250
I should just stay away from everyone.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.380
The boss is here.
Get up.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:47.540
Well, well, well, we meet again.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.250
The man from yesterday...

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.960
You know, I was planning to just run you over.

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:53.540
So, you were behind that runaway car.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:59.210
But then, I heard some interesting info
that made me want to kidnap you instead.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.040
Don't touch her.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.040
Excuse me?

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.040
If you let us go right now,
I'm prepared to overlook all this.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:08.210
You think you're real tough, huh?!

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:13.170
I dunno if you're some hotshot bodyguard or what,

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.710
but you need to learn when to shut the hell up!

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.000
I'll give you one more warning.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:26.170
Don't you lay your filthy hands on her.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:29.040
You just don't get it, do you?

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:30.790
Change of plans.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:35.420
I wasn't gonna kill you because I heard you'd make
for a good bargaining chip, but screw it.

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:36.040
Boss!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:39.670
Where exactly did you get this nonsensical,
wildly-incorrect intel of yours?

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.500
That's none of your business.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:44.500
Did it come from a teenage girl?

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.290
You're a dead man!

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.290
Teach!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.790
Magnificent.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.500
It was too well-executed to be a mere coincidence.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.330
For a supposed case of mistaken identity,

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.500
the countermeasures you used against me
were entirely too effective.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.080
Let me guess.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:15.920
After you failed to run this girl over,
you ran into a silver-haired girl wearing a ribbon.

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:21.580
That girl then fed you fake intel on us
under the guise of sharing rumors.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.630
Believing her, you decided to kidnap us.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:30.580
For your hostage, you chose a black-haired girl
you just happened to run across.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.500
And you learned our destination
from a girl with white hair.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:36.420
Is any of this ringing a bell?

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.290
How could you possibly...

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.460
This is quite impressive.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:44.830
In just ten days, you've all improved faster
than I could have ever imagined.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.960
It's no wonder I didn't notice.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.750
These man took their hostage in earnest,

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.000
and when they threatened us, they meant every word.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:53.460
It was a brilliant strategy.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.250
Wh-who is this guy?!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.960
What're you babbling about?!

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:58.460
This time, you're fuckin' dead!

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:00.420
There's just one thing I want to know.

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.500
How much longer should I keep
playing along with this game?

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:04.790
Attack!

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:32.460
If you think you can beat me, you're dreaming.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:41.040
I hit narcotic paydirt, yo!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.500
This will be enough to get them all arrested!

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.420
Wh-what's going on?!

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.130
You would think that playing the hostage
would be an easy role, but apparently not.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.460
I'm so sorry, Erna.

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:59.670
You gave us more good fortune than we planned for,

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.670
so we had to improvise on the fly.

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:04.540
We decided to bet on your ability!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.880
I mean, I did try to stop them.

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.330
I was like, think of how sad it'll make Erna!

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.580
Quit tryin' to cover your own ass.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:15.500
You should try working together with the others.

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:18.250
Lamplight's like me.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.380
The kind of misfortune you bring
isn't nearly enough to kill us.

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:22.880
He's got that right!

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:30.710
All right, Teach!
This time, we finally caught you!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.790
I could have died, you know.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.790
I'm sure it would take more than
a few bullets to kill you.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:37.830
Five minutes from now, the authorities will be here.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:39.460
You already made the call?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.670
Clever.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:44.130
At this rate, they're gonna haul you away, too.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:48.170
And what kind of pathetic spy gets questioned
by his own country's police?

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:52.670
I mean, if you say you surrender, then lick my boots
while calling me Lily the Great, I guess I could-

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:58.830
Those chains were designed for tying up big game...

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.830
You aren't qualified to be my enemies.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.790
How the hell did we still lose
after going to lengths like that?!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.960
I'm bummed out, yo.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.880
I guess that's Teach for you.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:21.540
First the combination lock, now the chains.
How does he do it?

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:22.830
That's a good question.

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.580
The strength it would have taken to
break through those big game chains...

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:27.210
I, um...

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:31.630
I know how he was able to destroy the chains.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:37.630
When we got captured, Teach used a jewel he had
hidden in his mouth to buy off one of the guards.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:38.920
How do you mean?

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:41.830
He got the man to damage the chains.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:46.670
Then, he intentionally provoked the guy in charge
to get him to open fire.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.380
So, he used the bullets to hit the weakened sections?

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:55.130
That would be enough to tear through any chains,
no matter how robust they were.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:58.420
I think he used the same trick to
open the combination lock.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:02.960
All he had to do was buy one of us off and
get them to tell him the code in advance.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.920
Y-you mean, one of us is a spy?!

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.750
We're all spies.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.250
Right, right...

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:11.630
Now that you mention it,

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:15.130
there was one person who always chimed in
whenever the topic of the lock came up.

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:19.790
Yeah, and someone who kept going on
about bonds and trusting each other!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.170
Hey, Lily, I've got a question for you.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.630
Where'd you get those financiers?

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:28.960
I was just...

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:31.420
Look, Teach basically made me do it!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.580
He said that I needed practice lying,

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:37.080
and you all needed practice doubting your allies.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.380
Wow, what a great leader,
accepting her friends' hatred for the good of the team!

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:44.290
It definitely wasn't the ridiculously-scrumptious
snacks that sealed the deal, no way!

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:50.960
Remember that whole thing about how we're spies,
and we can't afford to give out our trust so easily?

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:52.170
A-hem!

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:56.710
You know, I just got an idea.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:59.250
Wait, don't tell me...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.290
Teach, I just snatched up some information
you're gonna want to hear!

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:05.960
The others wrote out their whole plan.
Here, look!

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:07.790
Heh, you're wide open!

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.330
You got paint all over my maidenly nose!

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.250
That was awesome, yo!

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.790
Wh-What do you mean?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:19.420
They treated you like a washout at the academy,
but you're totally awesome!

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.920
I give you my praise, yo!

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:26.460
Well, of course I am.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:33.460
I guess I don't mind being your friend.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:37.920
H-how unlucky!

00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:13.920
I think I'm going to get along with the others.

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:15.210
I see.

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.790
It's all thanks to you, Teach.

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:20.380
I still have a lot to learn.

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:23.290
Are you ever going to finish that painting?

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:26.540
That's a fair question.

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:30.460
I bought all this new paint,
but it just isn't speaking to me.
